  "description": "Pawko is a pachinko board with a deck of cards over it. A round is five waves of balls: before each wave you play one of the five cards dealt for the level, and a card played is gone, so the whole game is choosing which power to spend when. Cards set random pegs on fire, freeze them, turn them into bumpers, magnets or bombs, double what the classic pegs pay, double the gates at the foot of the board or fatten every wave still to come. Then a tap on the board picks where the wave falls from, and every peg a ball rattles against pays a little, a burning or frozen ball pays more, a charged one pays double, and the gate each ball ends in adds a bonus or takes one away. The objective fills the board behind the pegs as the score climbs. Thirty levels, each asking for a higher score off the same board.",
